1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,066
DappGo existed before this hackathon.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:07,133
This verifier, its site and every piece of
evidence were built between October 27 and

3
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:07,800
November 4.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,833
A finance post goes viral.

5
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,266
Thousands repost it.

6
00:00:11,266 --> 00:00:12,133
Is it right?

7
00:00:12,133 --> 00:00:15,700
This one has a real number
— and the wrong period.

8
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,700
Numbers like this move money,
and wrong numbers lose it.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,466
And it's not just text.

10
00:00:22,466 --> 00:00:23,766
Screenshots,

11
00:00:23,766 --> 00:00:28,533
PDFs, podcasts, videos
— numbers everywhere.

12
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:31,700
How do you check all of them?

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,366
Asking a model directly
gets one in five right.

14
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,766
Give the same model SEC evidence,
and let a program decide:

15
00:00:39,766 --> 00:00:40,733
nine in ten —

16
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,233
on held-out claims, 240 of 266.

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:46,700
Here's how.

18
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:52,166
Meta's Muse Spark reads the post, extracts
each claim and chooses which SEC lookup to

19
00:00:52,166 --> 00:00:52,466
run.

20
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,966
Python does the arithmetic
and returns the verdict.

21
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,800
The model proposes; the program decides.

22
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,300
Live, on the site.

23
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,433
Paste the post.

24
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,233
Muse Spark calls the SEC tools.

25
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,166
Contradicted, with the filing.

26
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,300
And here is the corrected draft.

27
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,166
Apple's annual revenue was $416
billion; the quarter was $102.5 billion.

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,300
Every SEC call is on the record.

29
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,933
You can see each call.

30
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,166
Cost and time, on the receipt.

31
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,166
The same checks run in batch
from the command line — text,

32
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,100
screenshots through Muse OCR,

33
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,600
audio through Muse Voice Transcribe.

34
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,666
On saved Threads posts,
the median was 6.8 seconds.

35
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,366
At that median, a thousand posts
take about two hours on one worker.

36
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,833
Ninety point two percent
on held-out claims.

37
00:02:21,833 --> 00:02:25,366
It wrongly says 'supported' once in 139.

38
00:02:25,366 --> 00:02:28,333
Two cents and ten seconds a claim.

39
00:02:28,333 --> 00:02:33,700
On real posts, coverage is
reported separately from accuracy.

40
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:43,166
Every number, checked against the filing.

41
00:02:43,166 --> 00:02:49,700
hackathon dot dappgo dot com.

42
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,500
Built with Meta Muse Spark, on Baseten.

43
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,700
DappGo.

